# CSV parser — an M1 validation project (00 §33.1).
#
# A genuine M1 program over the frozen M1 surface only. It parses real CSV
# rows with a quote-parity state machine: splitting a row on commas gives
# pieces, and splitting a piece on `"` gives one fragment more than the
# quotes it holds — so an EVEN fragment count means the piece straddles a
# quote boundary. Inside quotes a comma belongs to the field; outside, it
# ends a field. Fields are re-marked with tab separators (a character CSV
# data never contains) so the render pass can split them apart again, which
# keeps empty fields intact. Rows are then validated against the header's
# width, so ragged rows are reported as refusals, not silently rendered.
# The same program must produce the same output through the interpreter and
# the native backend.

use files

kind field outcome
  is a good with cells of type a list of text and tally of type number
  is a bad with reason of type text

# ----- split one CSV row into its fields ---------------------------------------

function csv fields
  takes text called row
  returns a field outcome
  make parts equal to split row and ","
  make changing seen equal to ""
  make changing open equal to false
  make changing out equal to ""
  make changing started equal to false
  make changing n equal to 0
  repeat for each part in parts
    make marks equal to split part and "\""
    make width equal to size of marks
    make changing halved equal to width divided evenly by 2
    make changing twice equal to 2 times halved
    make toggles equal to twice is equal to width
    if open
      make changing joined equal to "{seen},{part}"
      set seen to joined
      if toggles
        set open to false
        if started
          make changing done equal to "{out}\t{seen}"
          set out to done
        otherwise
          set out to seen
        set started to true
        set seen to ""
        increase n by 1
    otherwise
      if toggles
        set seen to part
        set open to true
      otherwise
        if started
          make changing flat equal to "{out}\t{part}"
          set out to flat
        otherwise
          set out to part
        set started to true
        increase n by 1
  if open
    gives back a bad with reason "unterminated quoted field"
  make picked equal to split out and "\t"
  gives back a good with cells picked and tally (n)

# ----- validate one row against the header's width ------------------------------

function validate row
  takes text called raw
  takes number called want
  returns a field outcome
  make outcome equal to csv fields of raw
  match outcome
    when a good with cells cs and tally t
      if t is equal to want
        gives back a good with cells cs and tally (t)
      otherwise
        make changing note equal to "expected {want} fields, found {t}"
        gives back a bad with reason note
    when a bad with reason r
      gives back a bad with reason r

# ----- render one row ------------------------------------------------------------

function render cells
  takes a list of text called cells
  returns a text
  # `join` concatenates (the frozen text module's one join), so the table
  # renderer walks the cells and interposes the separator itself.
  make changing n equal to 0
  make changing line equal to ""
  repeat while n is less than size of cells
    if n is greater than 0
      make changing gap equal to "{line} | "
      set line to gap
    make cell equal to cells at n
    make changing line2 equal to "{line}{cell}"
    set line to line2
    increase n by 1
  gives back line

# ----- the main pipeline: read, parse, validate, render ---------------------

attempt open file "csv_input.csv" if it fails then
  say "cannot read the input: {problem}"
otherwise
  make all csv equal to result
  make raw rows equal to split all csv and "\n"
  make rows equal to keep raw rows using size of it is greater than 0
  say "records: {size of rows}"

  make header outcome equal to csv fields of (rows at 0)
  make changing want equal to 0
  make changing header bad equal to ""
  match header outcome
    when a good with cells cs and tally t
      set want to t
    when a bad with reason r
      set header bad to r

  if header bad is not equal to ""
    say "bad header: {header bad}"
  otherwise
    make changing rendered equal to ""
    make changing good count equal to 0
    make changing bad count equal to 0

    repeat for each r in rows
      make outcome equal to validate row of r and want
      match outcome
        when a good with cells cs and tally t
          make changing line equal to render cells of cs
          make changing marked equal to "{rendered}{line}\n"
          set rendered to marked
          increase good count by 1
        when a bad with reason reason
          say "bad row: {reason}"
          increase bad count by 1

    say rendered
    say "good rows: {good count}"
    say "bad rows: {bad count}"
